7 Affordable Fashion Brands Every College Girl Should Know
Looking good on a student budget is possible — you just need to know where to look. Here are seven brands that don't ask you to choose between style and your monthly allowance.
Meesho Fashion Finds — basics you'll wear on repeat, without the guilt of a big spend.
Bewakoof — graphic tees and oversized fits that don't take themselves too seriously.
Fabindia (sale season) — ethnic wear that lasts years, not just one wedding season.
Zara (end-of-season sale) — pricier, but the sale racks make it worth the wait.
Snitch — fast-moving trends at prices that don't punish you for keeping up.
Urbanic — new drops every week, so there's always something fresh.
Local thrift/Instagram resellers — one-of-a-kind pieces nobody else will be wearing.
You don't need a big wardrobe budget to have a wardrobe you're excited about — just a few reliable go-tos.
